Factorial (Iterative vs RecursivThis program calculates the factorial of a number (e.g., 5! = 5×4×3×2×1) two different ways:

-> Iterative: Uses a simple loop that multiplies numbers together one by one.
-> Recursive: The function calls itself repeatedly, breaking the problem into smaller pieces (like x! = x × (x−1)!) until it reaches the base case.
   Both methods give the same answer, but the program times each one separately (in nanoseconds) so you can compare their speed.
   
