practical 7

    Implementation of making a change problem using dynamic programmimg 

Summary: This program counts the number of ways to make a target amount using given coins,
via bottom-up DP where dp[i] tracks combinations for amount i — looping coins outer, amounts inner, to avoid counting order variations separately.

Conclusion: For coins {1,2,5} and amount 5, it outputs 4 ways, solving the problem efficiently in O(amount × coins) time instead of exponential brute force.
